# November 21, 2026: the District of Columbia, region dc, claimed with tools/choose.py --thinnest (19 places, all from
# batch dc_uzsg, mostly in Rock Creek Park, Georgetown and on the Mall). A second scatter across the District, east of
# the Anacostia and in Northeast as much as Northwest: the Capitol's old columns and the last brickworks at the National
# Arboretum, the Kenilworth lily ponds, the Franciscan Monastery, Cedar Hill, two Fort Circle earthworks east of the
# river, Woodlawn Cemetery, Eastern Market and the Old Naval Hospital on Capitol Hill, the cable-car barn by the Navy Yard,
# St. Paul's Rock Creek, Lincoln's Cottage, what is left of the McMillan sand filters, Rosedale, the Georgetown Reservoir
# castle gatehouse, the Mason house ruins on Theodore Roosevelt Island, the Octagon and the Renwick chapel at Oak Hill.
# Facts come from sources opened in this session: Wikipedia read as raw text (wiki_raw.py), National Park Service pages
# (nps.gov/places/..., planyourvisit and history pages, and each park's <code>_linked_data.json for opening hours, because
# the parks' hours pages draw them by script), and the pages of Lincoln's Cottage, the Franciscan Monastery, Oak Hill
# Cemetery, St. Paul's, the Rosedale Conservancy, Eastern Market and DC Parks and Recreation, read with tools/page.py.
# The National Arboretum's site and the Octagon's visiting page would not open, so their hours were not read.
